# The gear page draws the body (owner 2026-09-17): the player's own figure, not a
# wire outline, wearing what the loadout holds, scanned onto the slate's glass —
# and the same look on the figure walking the coast. Each piece is put on through
# the page's own key, and each frame is held to the world having it on (`worn:ID`
# asks the walking figure, which the page draws the same look as).
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/gear-figure.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 --held=pick --give=scanner_lens:1,oilskin:1,mitts_corded:1,glide_wing:1
coast calm
tap pause
choose loadout
tap use
await app:loadout 10
wait 0.8
shot 01-the-bare-body-on-the-gear-page with app:loadout
choose head
tap use
await worn:scanner_lens 6
wait 0.9
shot 02-a-scanner-lens-goes-on with app:loadout,worn:scanner_lens
choose body
tap use
await worn:oilskin 6
wait 0.9
shot 03-an-oilskin-over-it with app:loadout,worn:oilskin
choose hands
tap use
await worn:mitts_corded 6
wait 0.9
shot 04-corded-mitts with app:loadout,worn:mitts_corded
# The back slot turns the body round to show what is on its back.
choose back
tap use
await worn:glide_wing 6
wait 1.4
shot 05-turned-to-show-the-wing-on-its-back with app:loadout,worn:glide_wing
tap move_right
wait 0.9
shot 06-turned-round-by-hand with app:loadout
tap pause
tap pause
wait 1.0
zoom 5
wait 0.5
shot 07-the-same-kit-on-the-walking-figure with worn:oilskin,worn:mitts_corded,worn:scanner_lens
